{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"HB0157","billNumberShort":"H.B. 157","billNumberLong":"HB0157S03","fileNumber":"2026FL0568","shortTitle":"Department of Natural Resources Amendments","currentSubVersion":"3","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"SHIPPRP","primeSponsorName":"Rep. Shipp, Rex P.","primeSponsorHouse":"H","floorSponsor":"STRATKJ","floorSponsorName":"Sen. Stratton, Keven J.","floorSponsorHouse":"S","generalProvisions":"This bill addresses provisions related to the Department of Natural Resources.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>removes language related to determining the work period for certain Department of Natural Resources' employees;<hr><ltbullet>modifies provisions related to records kept by the Division of Water Rights, including to allow for the records to be kept in physical or electronic form;<hr><ltbullet>corrects citations;<hr><ltbullet>addresses treatment of water rights after termination or noncompliance of certain royalty contracts or mineral leases;<hr><ltbullet>removes a cap on low-interest loans related to secondary water metering;<hr><ltbullet>modifies when certain applications may be filed with the state engineer under instream flow provisions;<hr><ltbullet>clarifies rulemaking authority related to rules enforced by the Division of Law Enforcement;<hr><ltbullet>modifies the duties of the Utah Geological Survey;<hr><ltbullet>modifies the makeup of the Board of the Utah Geological Survey;<hr><ltbullet>changes the term \"buffalo\" to \"bison\" in certain circumstances;<hr><ltbullet>repeals section specifying funding sources of the Watershed Restoration Initiative;<hr><ltbullet>repeals the Alternative Energy Development Tax Credit Act; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical and conforming amendments.","moniesAppropriated":"","draftingAttorney":"Patricia Owen","fiscalAnalyst":"Lacey K. Moore","lastAction":"House/ filed","lastActionOwner":"House file for bills not passed","lastActionDate":"3/6/